%% Claim arbitration between two simultaneous identical requests (Google Sheets has no atomic upsert).
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant A as Execution A
  participant B as Execution B
  participant S as Sheet: claims
  participant L as Sheet: leads
  A->>L: look up submission (nothing yet)
  B->>L: look up submission (nothing yet)
  A->>S: append claim A
  B->>S: append claim B
  A->>S: read claims for this submission
  B->>S: read claims for this submission
  Note over A,B: Both see [A, B]. The first row in sheet order wins.
  A->>L: write status = recibido
  A-->>A: HTTP 202, call the model, score, save
  B->>L: look up again
  alt A already stored the lead
    B-->>B: HTTP 200 duplicate
  else A has not stored it yet (or died)
    B-->>B: HTTP 503 in progress, retry in 30 s
  end
